        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "RAY COOKE AUCTIONEERS are delighted to introduce 18 Griffeen Glen Crescent to the Lucan market. This fully rennovated semi-detatched family home consists of 3 double bedrooms, 3 bathrooms and an office/garden room to the rear. This property is nicely nestled in a quiet enclave, ideally located within the Griffeen Glen development. There are a number of amenities in the area including Liffey Valley Shopping Centre, Lucan Shopping Centre, Griffeen Valley Park and the new Lucan Swimming Pool and Gym which is accessible through the park's gate only a 2 min walk. There are several primary and secondary schools, supermarkets, shops, restaurants, bars, and cafes all in close proximity. The area is well catered for by public transportation with Kishoge train station being a 5-minute drive away and several bus stops in the locality. The N4 is minutes away and provides easy access to the M50, Dublin Airport, and Dublin City Centre.\nBright, spacious and light filled interior living accommodation of c. 100 sq.m comprises of an inviting entrance hallway that's opens into the cosy lounge room to the front with feature fireplace. The downstairs further consists of an open plan kitchen/ diner with an additional utility room and guest W.C. Upstairs boasts a main family bathroom and three spacious double bedrooms with the master benefiting of an ensuite. Externally to the rear you will find a low maintinance rear garden with a fabulous office/garden room which can be used for a variety of uses. Externally to the front you will find an extra wide front driveway for off-street parking.\nNo.18 comes to the market in fantastic condition throughout and boasts gas fired central heating, double glazed windows, utility room, rear office/garden room, XL front driveway and top quality flooring & fittings throughout. This fine family home is ideal for first time buyers and families looking to trade up. Early viewing is highly advised, Call Ray Cooke Auctioneers for further information or to arrange viewing on 01 403 0720.\n\nFeatures:\n-3 Bed/ 3 bath\n-TURN KEY Semi-deatched Family home\n-Rear office/ garden room\n-Fully renovated throughout\n-Gas fired central heating\n-Double glazed windows\n-Light filled interior\n-Feature fireplace in lounge\n-Wide front driveway for off street parking\n-Quiet development located in a cul de sac\n-Spacious room proportions\n-Within easy access to a host of shops and supermarkets\n-A host of transport links at your doorstep\n-Kishoge train station only a 5-minute drive away\n-Liffey Valley Shopping Centre within easy reach\n-Viewing highly advised!\n\nDirections:\nEircode = K78 R659"
      },
      {
